Problem Statement:
What problem did I solve?

Students think best when they write by hand, but everything else about their academic life happens on a screen. 
Assignments, revision, sharing and searching all live digitally, so their handwritten notes end up stuck in a format that doesn't fit. 
Every student feels this in the same small, repeating ways:

Carrying four or five heavy notebooks every day because they don't know which subject they'll need next.
Losing one notebook and losing weeks of notes with it, with no backup.
Spending an hour before exams photographing and scanning pages, just to get a searchable copy.
Having notes from different subjects scattered, with no organization unless the student sorts them by hand.
Turning those notes into practice questions or revision material by hand, when time is already short.

Current options don't solve this. Scanning apps only capture pages, so the student still has to organize and study from them manually. 
Fully digital note-taking asks students to give up the handwriting that helps them learn. The problem is not that students lack notes. 
Their notes are trapped, unorganized and unused, at exactly the moment they need them most.

Solution:
How does your application solve this problem?

Our web application lets students keep writing by hand and gives their notes a smart digital home. 
Students upload their handwritten pages as photos or scans, and the application does the rest:

Upload: The student uploads photos or scans of handwritten notes.
Convert: The application turns them into a clean, readable digital PDF that can be searched and shared.
Auto-organize: AI reads the content and files each document into the correct subject folder, so the student doesn't sort anything manually.
Access anywhere: All notes sit in one organized, searchable library, on any device, with no notebook needed for backup or revision.
Premium study tools: Premium users get quizzes, tasks and practice exams generated from their own stored notes, so revision starts from what they 
actually wrote instead of a blank page.

Outcome: Students keep the way they learn best, handwriting, and get organized, searchable, backed-up notes plus ready-made study material, 
with no manual sorting and no lost notebooks.

What Did I Build?

We built ScribeSync, a web application for students who take handwritten notes. Students upload photos or scans of their handwritten pages, 
and the app turns them into clean, searchable digital documents. AI then reads each document and files it into the right subject folder automatically, 
so nothing has to be sorted by hand. All notes end up in one organized library that students can open from any device, which means a lost notebook no 
longer means lost notes. A premium tier generates quizzes, tasks and practice exams from the student's own stored notes.

